{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The patch removes tenant scoping from a protected update operation, allowing authenticated users to modify another tenant's resource whenever IDs overlap.\n\nReview comment:\n\n- [P1] Keep tenant scope in the update predicate — /private/var/folders/xg/zvk2hrzx57s65nj22g15z1900000gn/T/native-review-feasibility-execution-a6z5m031/runs/R06/repo/update.go:16-16\n  When two tenants use the same resource ID, any authenticated tenant can now update the first matching row regardless of ownership because `authenticatedTenant` is discarded. The route contract explicitly permits tenant-local IDs to repeat and exposes this write operation to every authenticated tenant, so this enables cross-tenant modification; retain `TenantID == authenticatedTenant` in the lookup."}}
